**Read:** [Nonvolatile residue collection and analysis — Gordon, Rutherford and Aranda](../sources/Nonvolatile-Residue-Collection-and-Analysis-NASA.lingua#r_2YMCRSWR07NCHECM0X4D8FJ6HJ), the main method, analytical examples and relevant complete instrument appendix; [Cleaning and surface properties — Mauro Taborelli](../sources/Cleaning-and-Surface-Properties-Taborelli.lingua#r_1RDARBEFXDAW9Y2DNTJ2QBEP2E), independent surface/extract comparisons.

Choose a sampled object and intended function. Reconstruct the extraction, aliquots, blanks, mass difference, recovery and surface-area basis. Then distinguish chemical assignments from quantitative response. Identify material excluded or transformed by the preparation.

**Work:** Independently recompute a reported or explicitly hypothetical result with uncertainty and units. Use complementary chemical and surface observations to challenge a proposed residue identity. Compare a witness coupon with the actual geometry and exposure. Explain which evidence would establish a functional consequence and which only establishes an analytical result. Do not copy the report's ambiguous mass expression without deriving the accounting.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
